  "ownership": "CLI owns observation descriptors, not daemon resources. Each snapshot is revalidated after pidfd_open; all candidates pin before any signal. Partial admission failure drops all acquired descriptors without signalling. Success, signal/poll errors, caller cancellation and budget expiry close observation handles; native targets keep original resource owners and startup lease through their own drain. The daemon Stop path emits SIGTERM only. Existing capture-orphan retirement retains its separate escalation policy and tests. Handle count is bounded by candidate count and native descriptor admission; exhaustion fails before any signal.",
